server.add_tool(tool_customer_points_balance_lookup, name='customer_points_balance_lookup', description="Returns the exact current points balance for a single identified customer. Must match customer by email address or customer ID. Used by CSMs and merchants when helping an individual shopper resolve a points question or issue. This is exact or refuse\u2014no approximation.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Approximate or estimated balances** \u2192 This is exact or refuse. If customer not found, you get explicit refusal, never an estimate.\n- **Points balances for multiple customers at once** \u2192 Use \"Customer list export with filters\" instead (Entry #6). This is for one customer only.\n- **Historical balances for past dates** \u2192 Use \"Customer points history\" (Entry #3) to see balance at past dates. This shows current balance only.\n- **Points broken down by earning source** (purchase vs. referral vs. sign-up) \u2192 Use \"Points origin breakdown\" for aggregate analysis. For one customer's breakdown, use \"Customer points history\" (Entry #3) which shows each transaction's source.\n- **Custom points report by date ranges** \u2192 Use \"Customer points history\" (Entry #3) if you need \"points earned before X date, current balance, redeemed after Y date\". Evidence: Melinda Maria Designs - \"Need custom breakdown for expiration management.\"\n- **Why points haven't posted yet** \u2192 Use \"Transaction points details\" (Entry #5) instead. This shows current posted balance, not pending or problematic transactions.\n- **Points balance in dollars** \u2192 This returns points count. For dollar value, see redemption value in your program settings. For aggregate dollar liability, use \"Points activity and outstanding balance\" (Entry #14).\n- **Whether customer is \"close to\" redeeming** \u2192 Subjective interpretation. This gives exact balance; you decide what \"close to\" means for your reward thresholds.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- customer_identifier (required): email address OR customer ID\n- include_pending (optional): whether to show pending points\n- include_expiring (optional): whether to show points expiring soon with dates")

