server.add_tool(tool_customer_list_export, name='customer_list_export', description="Generates a downloadable file (CSV) containing exact customer loyalty data matching specified filters. Returns exact data for all customers who meet the criteria at time of export. Used by merchants for email campaigns, financial reporting, CRM syncs, and bulk analysis. This is bulk exact-data operation\u2014returns actual customer records, not analytics or estimates.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Exports without any criteria** \u2192 Must specify at least time range OR segment OR tier. Prevents accidental \"export everyone\" which may be too large.\n- **Customer data outside loyalty domain** \u2192 Payment info (Shopify), shipping addresses (PII beyond loyalty), order details beyond points activity (Shopify). This exports loyalty data only: points, tiers, membership info.\n- **Real-time/live data feeds** \u2192 This is a point-in-time snapshot at time of export generation. For live sync, use ESP integration settings.\n- **Exports exceeding 50,000 customers** \u2192 Requires support for large exports (file size, processing time). This is self-serve up to 50K rows.\n- **Scheduled or recurring exports** \u2192 Product feature, not a query. Use export scheduler in dashboard if available.\n- **Exports where count matches dashboard UI display** \u2192 Evidence: Scamp and Dude - \"95k in file vs. 139k shown in UI.\" **This export count is accurate** (verified source data). If it differs from UI, the export is correct\u2014UI may show cached/stale count. Preview step shows verified count before generation.\n- **Klaviyo sync validation** (who was synced when) \u2192 Evidence: Earth Therapeutics - \"Need to know which customers were synced for reconciliation.\" That's integration sync logging, not export. Use ESP integration health report if available.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- filter_criteria (required): at minimum, specify time range OR segment OR tier OR points range\n  - tier: filter by tier name(s)\n  - points_min / points_max: points balance range\n  - join_date_start / join_date_end: when they joined loyalty\n  - last_activity_start / last_activity_end: when they last earned/redeemed\n  - segment: predefined segment name\n  - days_inactive: customers with no activity for X+ days\n- fields (optional): which columns to include (defaults to standard set: ID, email, points, tier, join date, last activity)\n- format (optional): CSV (default) or JSON\n- sort_by (optional): how to sort rows (points desc, join_date asc, etc.)")

