server.add_tool(tool_average_order_value_by_segment, name='average_order_value_by_segment', description="Returns the average order value (AOV) for customers in a specified segment **for a time period** (week, month, quarter, year, custom range). Handles comparisons across segments (e.g., \"ALM vs non-ALM AOV in Q2\") and across time periods. Used by merchants to understand spending behavior and measure loyalty program lift. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **AOV for individual customers** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) for one customer's purchase data. This is segment-level aggregate.\n- **AOV for specific products or categories** \u2192 Product analytics, not loyalty analytics. This is AOV by customer segment, not by product.\n- **AOV for specific campaigns** \u2192 Use campaign performance entry if available. This is segment-level, not campaign-specific.\n- **Predictions about future AOV** \u2192 This is historical/current aggregate. Cannot predict future behavior.\n- **Prescriptive advice about how to increase AOV** \u2192 This gives you the data (which segments spend more). You decide strategy.\n- **Pre-discount AOV for incrementality analysis** \u2192 Evidence: Travis Mathew - \"Need pre-discount AOV to prove incrementality to finance teams.\" This returns post-discount AOV (actual transaction amount). For pre-discount analysis, that's a separate metric (would need new entry).\n- **Why AOV differs between segments** \u2192 This shows the numbers (difference). Causal analysis (why) is prescriptive/analytical beyond data reporting.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- segment (required): which segment (ALM, non-ALM, tier name, redeemers, non-redeemers)\n- time_range (required): date range for analysis\n- comparison_segment (optional): compare to another segment (e.g., \"vs. non-ALM\")\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- include_trend (optional): show trend over time")

