server.add_tool(tool_tier_movement_summary, name='tier_movement_summary', description="Returns the number and percentage of customers who moved between tiers during a **past** time period. Shows upgrades, downgrades, and retention (stayed in same tier). Includes tier progression metrics like time to upgrade and net retention rate. Used by merchants to understand tier dynamics and program health. This is historical data\u2014for future tier risk, use \"At-risk tier customers\" instead. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Who will drop a tier in the future** \u2192 Use \"At-risk tier customers\" for customers likely to downgrade. Evidence: Frank & Eileen - \"Need report showing expected tier shifts due to expiring points.\" This entry shows what DID happen, not what WILL happen.\n- **Which specific customers moved tiers** \u2192 Use \"Customer list export\" (Entry #6) filtered by tier change date for customer names/emails. This returns counts only.\n- **Why customers moved tiers** \u2192 This shows counts and rates (data). Reasons are: achieved spending threshold, points expired, anniversary reset, etc. (policy-driven, not data query).\n- **Whether tier thresholds are \"right\"** \u2192 Prescriptive advice about program design, out of scope. This gives you movement data; you decide if thresholds need adjustment.\n- **Individual customer's tier history** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) or \"Customer points history\" (Entry #3) for one customer's tier over time. This is aggregate movement counts.\n- **Tier distribution at historical date** \u2192 Use \"Historical tier distribution snapshot\" for state (counts at point in time). This shows movement (events: who upgraded/downgraded), not state.\n- **Predictions about future tier movements** \u2192 This is historical data. Cannot predict future upgrades/downgrades.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- time_range (required): date range for analysis (historical period)\n- tier_name (optional): focus on specific tier (e.g., \"who upgraded to Gold?\")\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- include_trend (optional): show trend over time\n- include_time_to_upgrade (optional): show average days to upgrade")

