server.add_tool(tool_purchase_frequency_by_segment, name='purchase_frequency_by_segment', description="Returns the average number of orders per customer for a specified segment **for a time period** (week, month, quarter, year, custom range). Handles comparisons across segments (e.g., \"ALM vs non-ALM in Q4\") and across time periods. Shows how frequently customers purchase, not whether they repeat (that's repeat purchase rate). Used by merchants to understand purchase behavior patterns and measure loyalty program impact on shopping frequency. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Repeat purchase rate** (binary: did they buy more than once?) \u2192 Use \"Repeat purchase rate by segment\" (Entry #11). This returns average order count, that returns percentage who repeated.\n- **Individual customer's order count** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) for one customer's order history. This is segment-level aggregate.\n- **Total orders placed** (volume, not per-customer average) \u2192 This is frequency (orders per customer), not total volume. For volume: order count is in behavioral summaries.\n- **Predictions about future purchase frequency** \u2192 This is historical/current aggregate. Cannot predict future behavior.\n- **Why frequency differs between segments** \u2192 This shows the numbers (difference). Causal analysis (why) is prescriptive beyond data reporting.\n- **Which products customers buy** \u2192 Product analytics. This is purchase frequency (how often), not product mix (what they buy).\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- segment (required): which segment (ALM, non-ALM, tier name, redeemers, non-redeemers)\n- time_range (required): date range for analysis\n- comparison_segment (optional): compare to another segment (e.g., \"vs. non-ALM\")\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- include_trend (optional): show trend over time")

