server.add_tool(tool_at_risk_tier_customers, name='at_risk_tier_customers', description="Returns list of customers who will drop to a lower tier in the near future **within a specified risk window** (e.g., next 30/60/90 days). **A customer is at risk if:** (1) their points are expiring soon and they'll fall below tier threshold, (2) their tier anniversary period is ending without sufficient qualifying activity, or (3) they have insufficient qualifying spend to maintain tier status. Used for proactive retention campaigns and customer success outreach. Evidence: Frank & Eileen - \"Need report showing expected tier shifts due to expiring points.\" This is predictive\u2014for historical tier changes, use \"Tier movement summary\" instead. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable (timing estimates may vary).\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Historical tier downgrades that already happened** \u2192 Use \"Tier movement summary\" (Entry #13) instead. This shows future risk, that shows past events.\n- **Why tier thresholds are set at current levels** \u2192 Policy question, not data query. This shows who's at risk given current thresholds.\n- **Whether to change tier thresholds** \u2192 Prescriptive advice, out of scope. This gives you the data (who's at risk), you decide tier strategy.\n- **Individual customer's full tier history** \u2192 Use \"Customer tier status lookup\" (Entry #2) or \"Customer points history\" (Entry #3) for one customer. This is aggregate risk list.\n- **How to prevent tier drops** \u2192 Prescriptive advice about retention tactics. This gives you the data (who's at risk), you decide the campaign strategy.\n- **Tier retention rate** \u2192 Use \"Tier movement summary\" (Entry #13) for retention metrics. This is about future risk, that's about past retention.\n- **Which customers will upgrade** \u2192 This is downgrade risk only. Upgrade prediction would be separate analysis (customer approaching next tier threshold).\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- risk_window_days (required): how far ahead to look (e.g., 30, 60, 90 days)\n- tier_filter (optional): specific tier to check\n- min_risk_amount (optional): only show if losing X+ points\n- sort_by (optional): days_until_downgrade (default), points_at_risk, tier\n- include_customer_list (optional): return customer names/emails or just count (default: count only for privacy)")

