server.add_tool(tool_average_revenue_per_customer_by_segment, name='average_revenue_per_customer_by_segment', description="Returns the average total revenue per customer from a specified segment **for a time period** (week, month, quarter, year, custom range). This is unit economics\u2014\"what's the average customer in this segment worth?\" not \"how much total revenue did the segment generate?\". Handles comparisons across segments (e.g., \"Gold vs Silver customer value\") and across time periods. Used by merchants and executives to understand customer value by segment and prioritize retention/acquisition investments. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Total revenue from segment** \u2192 Use \"Revenue by segment\" (Entry #9) for \"How much did Gold tier generate?\". This shows per-customer average, not total dollars.\n- **Revenue from individual customers** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) for one customer's total revenue. This is segment-level average.\n- **Customer lifetime value (LTV) prediction** \u2192 This is realized revenue to date (historical), not predicted future value (modeling). For realized LTV since joining, use \"Customer lifetime value\" (Entry #20).\n- **Revenue per order (AOV)** \u2192 Use \"Average order value\" (Entry #10). This is total revenue per customer (all orders), not average per single order.\n- **Profit or margin per customer** \u2192 Revenue only, not costs or profit. Loyalty platform tracks revenue, not full P&L.\n- **Why certain segments have higher customer value** \u2192 This shows the numbers (difference). Causal analysis (why) is prescriptive beyond data reporting.\n- **Which customers should be prioritized** \u2192 Prescriptive advice about resource allocation. This gives you customer value data; you decide prioritization based on value, cost to serve, retention risk, etc.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- segment (required): which segment (ALM, non-ALM, tier name, redeemers, non-redeemers)\n- time_range (required): date range for analysis\n- comparison_segment (optional): compare to another segment\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- include_trend (optional): show revenue per customer over time")

