server.add_tool(tool_loyalty_program_roi_summary, name='loyalty_program_roi_summary', description="Returns overall return on investment metrics for the loyalty program. Shows revenue from loyalty members vs. non-members, member behavior lift (AOV, purchase frequency), and engagement indicators. Used by executives, CFOs, and marketing teams to justify program investment and measure program health. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable, not exact customer-level accounting.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Specific customer-level ROI** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) for one customer's behavior. This is program-level aggregate.\n- **Dollar cost of rewards or point liability valuation** \u2192 Use \"Points activity and outstanding balance\" (Entry #14) for points data. For financial liability (dollar value), use points liability report (separate entry). Evidence: multiple merchants need liability for GAAP/IFRS.\n- **Prescriptive advice about how to improve ROI** \u2192 This gives you the data (current performance). You decide strategy changes. Out of scope: \"should I spend more on loyalty?\"\n- **Comparison to other merchants or industry benchmarks** \u2192 Multi-tenant data isolation. Cannot show other merchants' data. This shows YOUR performance only.\n- **ROI for specific campaigns** \u2192 Use campaign attribution entry if available. This is overall program ROI, not campaign-specific.\n- **Pre-discount AOV** for proving incrementality \u2192 Evidence: Travis Mathew - \"Need pre-discount AOV to prove incrementality to finance teams.\" This returns standard AOV. For pre-discount analysis, that's a separate metric (may need new entry).\n- **Why ROI changed** \u2192 This shows the data (revenue, behavior). Causal analysis (why it changed) is prescriptive/analytical beyond data reporting.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- time_range (required): date range for analysis\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- segment (optional): narrow to specific tier or member type\n- include_incremental_calculation (optional): show how incremental revenue is calculated")

