server.add_tool(tool_customer_count_by_segment, name='customer_count_by_segment', description="Returns the number of customers in a specified segment **for a time period** (point-in-time snapshot OR growth over a range). Shows current membership size and distribution, not new signups. Handles comparisons across time periods (e.g., \"How many ALMs in Q1 vs Q4?\"). Segments include: total loyalty members (ALM), tier membership, redeemers, repeat customers, purchasing customers. Used by merchants and CSMs to understand program size, tier distribution, and segment composition. This is analytical counting\u2014minor variations acceptable (e.g., customers who just joined might take minutes to appear).\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Individual customer identities** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) for one customer. This is aggregate count.\n- **List of customers in segment** \u2192 Use \"Customer list export\" (Entry #6) to get customer names/emails. This returns count only.\n- **How many new customers joined the program** \u2192 Use \"Customer acquisition rate\" (Entry #21) for new signups over time. This shows current membership (stock), that shows new joins (flow).\n- **Predictions about future segment size** \u2192 This is historical/current count. Cannot predict future.\n- **Detailed behavior within segments** \u2192 Use behavioral metric entries (AOV, repeat rate, etc.) for behavior analysis. This is count only.\n- **Cross-merchant comparisons** \u2192 Multi-tenant isolation. Cannot show other merchants' counts.\n- **How many customers in each tier made a purchase** \u2192 Evidence: AMOREPACIFIC - \"Need to differentiate between total members in a tier and those actively making purchases.\" That's \"Purchasing customers by tier\" (Entry #17). This shows total tier membership, not active purchasers.\n- **Why segment size changed** \u2192 This shows the count and trend. Causal analysis (why) is prescriptive/analytical beyond counting.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- segment (required): which segment to count\n  - Options: ALM (active loyalty members), specific tier name, redeemers, repeat customers, purchasing customers\n- time_range (required): date range for counting\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- include_trend (optional): show count over time (time series)\n- breakdown (optional): for \"tier\", show count for each tier separately")

