server.add_tool(tool_revenue_by_segment, name='revenue_by_segment', description="Returns total revenue from a specified customer segment **for a time period** (week, month, quarter, year, custom range). Shows aggregate dollars the segment generated, not per-customer averages. Handles comparisons across segments (e.g., \"ALM vs non-ALM in Q1 2025\") and across time periods. Segments include: loyalty members (ALM) vs. non-members, redeemers vs. non-redeemers, by tier, by repeat customer status. Used by merchants and executives to understand which segments drive revenue and measure loyalty program impact. This is aggregate analytical data\u2014slight variations acceptable.\n\nDOES NOT ANSWER / BOUNDARIES:\n- **Revenue from individual customers** \u2192 Use \"Customer loyalty profile\" (Entry #4) or \"Customer list export\" (Entry #6) for individual customer data. This is aggregate by segment.\n- **Average revenue per customer** \u2192 Use \"Average revenue per customer by segment\" (Entry #22) for unit economics (\"What's the average customer worth?\"). This shows total revenue (\"How much did the segment generate?\"), not per-customer averages.\n- **Revenue from specific products or categories** \u2192 Product analytics, not loyalty analytics. This is revenue by customer segment, not by product.\n- **Revenue from specific campaigns** \u2192 Use campaign attribution entry if available. This is segment-level, not campaign-specific.\n- **Prescriptive advice about how to increase revenue** \u2192 This gives you the data (which segments generate revenue). You decide strategy.\n- **Profit or margin data** \u2192 Revenue only, not costs or profit. Loyalty platform tracks revenue, not full P&L.\n- **\"Actual revenue\" vs. \"added revenue\" distinction** \u2192 Evidence: Murad - \"Dashboard doesn't provide actual revenue, only added revenue.\" This entry returns **actual revenue** (what the segment spent). For \"added revenue\" (incremental lift calculation), specify in parameters or use ROI entry.\n- **Pre-discount revenue** \u2192 Evidence: Travis Mathew - \"Need pre-discount AOV to prove incrementality.\" This returns post-discount revenue (actual transaction amount). Pre-discount would need separate entry or parameter.\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- segment (required): which segment (ALM, non-ALM, redeemers, non-redeemers, specific tier name, repeat customers)\n- time_range (required): date range for analysis\n- comparison_segment (optional): compare to another segment (e.g., \"vs. non-ALM\")\n- comparison_period (optional): compare to previous period, YoY, QoQ\n- include_trend (optional): show revenue over time (time series)\n- revenue_type (optional): \"actual\" (default - what they spent) or \"added\" (incremental lift calculation)")


